  {
    id: "porter-cable-7800",
    name: "Porter-Cable 7800",
    category: "Long Reach, 4.7 Amp, Variable Speed, Vacuum Ready",
    badge: "Best Value Professional",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.5,
    reviewCount: 4200,
    pros: [
      "Well proven professional machine at a fraction of premium pricing",
      "Variable speed across a genuinely useful range",
      "Articulating head follows the wall surface",
      "Good dust extraction when paired with a decent shop vacuum",
      "Widely available with cheap and easy sanding discs",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Heavier than premium machines, which tells over a full day",
      "Extraction is good rather than exceptional",
      "Vacuum hose adds drag that makes the tool feel heavier still",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The machine most drywall contractors actually own. Not the best at anything, competent at everything, sensibly priced.",
    description:
      "For a very long time this was the default powered drywall sander on job sites, and it retains that position for straightforward reasons: it works, it is affordable, and consumables are available everywhere. The articulating head follows the wall as your arms move, variable speed lets you back off on soft compound to avoid digging in, and dust extraction through a standard shop vacuum captures most of what the sanding produces. That combination covers the job properly without any single standout feature. Where it shows its age is weight. It is heavier than the premium machines and the balance is less refined, which is a minor observation on a small job and a significant one across a full day of ceilings. The vacuum hose attached to a long tool adds drag that compounds the effect, and by mid afternoon your shoulders will know about it. Extraction is good rather than exceptional. In our dust weighing the escape was noticeably higher than the Festool, though far better than any handheld option, and the room still needed a proper clean afterwards. Sanding discs are inexpensive and stocked widely, which matters because drywall sanding gets through them. For a contractor or a serious renovator, this is the sensible purchase.",
  },
  {
    id: "wen-6369",
    name: "WEN 6369 Variable Speed Drywall Sander",
    category: "Long Reach, 5 Amp, Variable Speed, Dust Hose Included",
    badge: "Best Budget",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.3,
    reviewCount: 12800,
    pros: [
      "Very low price for a full length powered drywall sander",
      "Variable speed control included",
      "Comes with a dust hose and collection bag",
      "Adequate performance for a single renovation project",
