    category: "Long Reach, 7 Amp, LED Ring, Foldable Handle",
    badge: "Best Lighting",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 9100,
    pros: [
      "LED ring around the sanding head reveals imperfections you would otherwise miss",
      "Foldable handle makes storage and transport far easier",
      "Strong motor with good speed range",
      "Detachable head for close-to-edge sanding",
      "Includes a generous set of sanding discs",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Heavier than it looks once the extension is fitted",
      "Dust collection is average and needs a vacuum",
      "LED adds another component that can fail",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The light is not a gimmick. Raking illumination shows the ridges you cannot see under normal room lighting.",
    description:
      "The reason drywall finishing looks perfect until the paint goes on is that ordinary room lighting is diffuse and hides surface irregularities completely. Professionals use a work light held at a shallow angle to the wall for exactly this reason, because raking light casts shadows from ridges and hollows that are otherwise invisible. The YATTICH builds a ring of LEDs around the sanding head, so the light is always at the right angle right where you are working. It sounds like a marketing feature and it is genuinely useful, particularly for someone doing this for the first time who does not yet know what to look for. Beyond the light, the machine is a competent mid-range tool. The motor is strong, the speed range is useful, the head detaches for sanding close to edges and corners, and the folding handle makes a long awkward tool storable. A generous set of discs is included, which offsets some of the price. The weaknesses are familiar. It is heavier than it appears once assembled, dust collection through the bag is unremarkable and needs a vacuum to be acceptable, and the LED ring is one more thing that can stop working. As a first drywall sander for a homeowner, it is a strong choice.",
